## Verified cause and correction

Original Rule::Cache requires a Set-typed rule trunk, a Setting-typed tag and
registered pattern/setting codenames. The modal fixture's layout tag had
neither a Setting type nor its `layout` codename. The qualified lookup
therefore excludes the intended Probe Layout and renders the code-default
layout, which asks for `header` that this minimal fixture does not contain.

The fixture helper already stores its replacement `*all` as the stock Set
type, despite the explicit Basic type in the caller's seed. The new positive
control queries this actual stored row and checks it against the registered
Set ID; no assumption about the caller's arguments supplies this fact.

The sole original-file hunk adds a registered Setting type and types/codenames
the `*layout` tag accordingly. The layout content, readable page content,
rule sides, board permission decision, expected HTML and HTTP status stay
unchanged. No `header` card is inserted to hide the wrong layout selection.

The original file's raw Git SHA-256 is
`165918662802f0bb5db3b6a075e7132e3e0be061d891602e3681ea3d980981b1`.
A whole-file comparison, normalizing line endings, proves every byte outside
the one layout seed replacement remains identical to the exact base. All
20 original test bodies and assertions are preserved. The database schema
also matches the base exactly. No runtime, shared seed constructor, lookup,
permission or normalization code changes.

