then compares actual `findRule` selection against that result. Four cases cover
the valid layout, a wrong Setting type, a wrong Set type, and a missing setting
codename. All malformed forms remain excluded. The original cache source was
read and hash-checked directly:
`17a240a32aed7c2ea07c69df21bfb78190a4cd501583171f2b23403de1f7736d`.
These new checks execute the ported SQL and original-derived key construction;
they do not claim a fresh Ruby/Rails/ActiveRecord execution.

The compiler runs in its own checked native subprocess: status zero,
signal/error null, empty diagnostics. No subsequent shell command masks it.
The explicit two-file platform scan has zero command landmines. Whitespace
validation passes. No full gate was run and no security assertion was relaxed.

